From 32a25f379015b09ee25eb5c9ae97c2cd41d5ab2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hank Yeomans <hank@quorra.ah.local>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 22:03:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/54] E20: tuned W8A8 block-FP8 [32,32] configs for RTX PRO
 6000 Max-Q (7 V4.1-Flash TP2 dense shapes) and let SM120 use the
 SPLIT_K/SWAP_AB kernel

Default config ran the dense GEMMs at 60-80 GB/s (3 % occupancy, 40 ms of a 70 ms
decode step). Tuned by kernels/e20/tune_w8a8_block32.py in the recipe repo:
M=1 5.6-12x faster, M=4 2.7-5.6x, M=4096 2.2-3.0x; every config checked against
an FP32 dequantised reference.

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a0c10b-a5f8-77fc-b238-7147d12ccf29
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
